  "description": "An eland in shaded red and white on a sandstone shelter in the Drakensberg, painted by the San with a fine brush and a polychrome technique that modelled the animal's bulk. The eland is the animal that appears most often in San painting; it was the creature of greatest spiritual power, and the trance dance of the healers drew on its potency.",
  "facts": [
   "The Drakensberg holds some 35,000 to 40,000 painted images in over 600 shelters.",
   "Most of the paintings are less than 2,000 years old and some show horses and guns from the 1800s.",
   "The park was listed as a World Heritage Site in 2000."
